---The properties of a managed instance.
---@class azure.sql.ManagedInstanceProperties
---@field provisioningState? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesProvisioningState The ARM provisioning state of the job execution.
---@field managedInstanceCreateMode? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesManagedInstanceCreateMode Specifies the mode of database creation. Default: Regular instance creation. Restore: Creates an instance by restoring a set of backups to specific point in time. RestorePointInTime and SourceManagedInstanceId must be specified.
---@field fullyQualifiedDomainName? string The fully qualified domain name of the managed instance.
---@field isGeneralPurposeV2? boolean Whether or not this is a GPv2 variant of General Purpose edition.
---@field administratorLogin? string Administrator username for the managed instance. Can only be specified when the managed instance is being created (and is required for creation).
---@field administratorLoginPassword? distilled.Secret The administrator login password (required for managed instance creation).
---@field subnetId? string Subnet resource ID for the managed instance.
---@field state? string The state of the managed instance.
---@field licenseType? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesLicenseType The license type. Possible values are 'LicenseIncluded' (regular price inclusive of a new SQL license) and 'BasePrice' (discounted AHB price for bringing your own SQL licenses).
---@field hybridSecondaryUsage? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesHybridSecondaryUsage Hybrid secondary usage. Possible values are 'Active' (default value) and 'Passive' (customer uses the secondary as Passive DR).
---@field hybridSecondaryUsageDetected? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesHybridSecondaryUsageDetected Hybrid secondary usage detected. Possible values are 'Active' (customer does not meet the requirements to use the secondary as Passive DR) and 'Passive' (customer meets the requirements to use the secondary as Passive DR).
---@field vCores? number The number of vCores. Allowed values: 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 56, 64, 80, 96, 128. Supported vCores depends on the selected hardware family and service tier.
---@field storageSizeInGB? number Storage size in GB. Minimum value: 32. Maximum value: 32768. Increments of 32 GB allowed only. Maximum value depends on the selected hardware family and number of vCores.
---@field storageIOps? number Storage IOps. Minimum value: 300. Maximum value: 80000. Increments of 1 IOps allowed only. Maximum value depends on the selected hardware family and number of vCores.
---@field storageThroughputMBps? number Storage throughput MBps parameter is not supported in the instance create/update operation.
---@field memorySizeInGB? number Memory size in GB. Minimum value: 28. Maximum value: 870. Minimum and maximum value depend on the number of vCores and service tier. Read more about resource limits: https://aka.ms/mi-resource-limits-api.
---@field collation? string Collation of the managed instance.
---@field dnsZone? string The Dns Zone that the managed instance is in.
---@field dnsZonePartner? string The resource id of another managed instance whose DNS zone this managed instance will share after creation.
---@field publicDataEndpointEnabled? boolean Whether or not the public data endpoint is enabled.
---@field sourceManagedInstanceId? string The resource identifier of the source managed instance associated with create operation of this instance.
---@field restorePointInTime? string Specifies the point in time (ISO8601 format) of the source database that will be restored to create the new database.
---@field proxyOverride? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesProxyOverride Connection type used for connecting to the instance.
---@field timezoneId? string Id of the timezone. Allowed values are timezones supported by Windows. Windows keeps details on supported timezones, including the id, in registry under KEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Time Zones. You can get those registry values via SQL Server by querying SELECT name AS timezone_id FROM sys.time_zone_info. List of Ids can also be obtained by executing [System.TimeZoneInfo]::GetSystemTimeZones() in PowerShell. An example of valid timezone id is "Pacific Standard Time" or "W. Europe Standard Time".
---@field instancePoolId? string The Id of the instance pool this managed server belongs to.
---@field maintenanceConfigurationId? string Specifies maintenance configuration id to apply to this managed instance.
---@field privateEndpointConnections? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesPrivateEndpointConnectionsList List of private endpoint connections on a managed instance.
---@field minimalTlsVersion? string Minimal TLS version. Allowed values: 'None', '1.0', '1.1', '1.2'
---@field currentBackupStorageRedundancy? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesCurrentBackupStorageRedundancy The storage account type used to store backups for this database.
---@field requestedBackupStorageRedundancy? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesRequestedBackupStorageRedundancy The storage account type used to store backups for this database.
---@field zoneRedundant? boolean Whether or not the zone-redundancy is enabled.
---@field primaryUserAssignedIdentityId? string The resource id of a user assigned identity to be used by default.
---@field keyId? string A CMK URI of the key to use for encryption.
---@field administrators? azure.sql.ManagedInstanceExternalAdministrator The Azure Active Directory administrator can be utilized during instance creation and for instance updates, except for the azureADOnlyAuthentication property. To update the azureADOnlyAuthentication property, individual API must be used.
---@field servicePrincipal? azure.sql.ServicePrincipal The managed instance's service principal.
---@field virtualClusterId? string Virtual cluster resource id for the Managed Instance.
---@field externalGovernanceStatus? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesExternalGovernanceStatus Status of external governance.
---@field pricingModel? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesPricingModel Pricing model of Managed Instance.
---@field createTime? string Specifies the point in time (ISO8601 format) of the Managed Instance creation.
---@field authenticationMetadata? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesAuthenticationMetadata The managed instance's authentication metadata lookup mode.
---@field databaseFormat? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesDatabaseFormat Specifies the internal format of instance databases specific to the SQL engine version.
---@field requestedLogicalAvailabilityZone? azure.sql.ManagedInstancePropertiesRequestedLogicalAvailabilityZone Specifies the availability zone the database is pinned to.

